# NOT ANONYMOUSLY PULLABLE. Measured 2026-09-05: an unauthenticated manifest request
# for this tag returns 401, so a host without a quay credential cannot stage this step,
# and the failure lands wherever the task was drawn rather than in front of whoever
# caused it. Nothing in ninety env files said so until curation round 6, which is why
# this comment exists rather than a schema key -- there is no key for it, and adding one
# the parser ignores would be worse.
# Whether the image exists could not be established here: the push credential this host
# carries has no read scope on the repository, so an authenticated request returns 404
# too, and 404 does not distinguish "absent" from "not granted". Someone with org read
# should confirm the tag before this env is relied on.
#
# TWO further problems on the same line, independent of each other and of the above.
# `:latest` is the ONLY floating tag in ninety env files: what it resolves to changes
# under every solve, and the method id this env feeds hashes the URI, not the image, so
# a silent swap is invisible. And `txyliu/` is a PERSONAL namespace, not `hallamlab/`,
# so the library's only route to this tool depends on one person's account.
#
# It also carries NO `conda:` line, so under the MAMBA runtime the staging preflight now
# refuses it by name -- correctly: there is no form of this step a container-less agent
# can run.
container: docker://quay.io/txyliu/pathologic:latest
